# 0087 — Windows: a child process is asked to stop before it is ended, and an argument `cmd.exe` cannot read is refused

Status: todo
Target: 0.8.0
Related: [[HQL-0064]], its companion note
[child processes](../proposals/HQL-0064/parts/02-child-processes.hmd), the
[I/O FAQ](../proposals/HQL-0064/parts/faq.hmd),
[[0085-hql-0064-beyond-child-processes|issue 0085]],
`src/process.rs`, `crates/hql-sys`

The companion note [child
processes](../proposals/HQL-0064/parts/02-child-processes.hmd) is
implemented on Linux, macOS and Windows except for two Windows rules. This
issue carries them. With it, the note is implemented in full on every
platform.

## Expected

| Case | Unix today | Windows today | Windows expected |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `hql` ends a child: `timeout_ms`, an unread stream, a signal to `hql` | `SIGTERM` to the group, `SIGKILL` after 5 seconds | `TerminateJobObject` at once | a graceful stop, then `TerminateJobObject` after 5 seconds |
| an argument of a `.bat` or `.cmd` program that `cmd.exe` cannot read as one argument | not applicable | passed on, quoted by the C runtime's rules | the evaluation failure `invalid-argument`, naming the argument |

- **The graceful stop.** `hql` sends Ctrl-Break to a console child, which
  it starts with a console process group of its own, and `WM_CLOSE` to
  each top-level window of a process in the child's Job Object. A child
  still running after 5 seconds, the `GRACE` of `src/process.rs`, is
  ended by `TerminateJobObject`.
- **The reason stays the same.** A child that `hql` stopped reports the
  same reason as on Unix (`timed-out`), whether the graceful stop ended it
  or `TerminateJobObject` did. Windows sets no `signal`.
- **The `cmd.exe` refusal.** A `program` ending in `.bat` or `.cmd` is run
  by `cmd.exe`. An argument that `hql` cannot quote so that `cmd.exe` reads
  it as one argument, such as one holding `"`, `%`, `^`, `&`, `|`, `<`, `>`
  or a line break, is `invalid-argument`, and the child does not start.

## Where

- Ctrl-Break needs `CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP` at spawn and
  `GenerateConsoleCtrlEvent`. Enumerating a job's processes and their
  windows, and posting `WM_CLOSE`, need `unsafe`. That code goes into
  `crates/hql-sys`, behind a safe API, as the note requires. The `hql`
  crate keeps `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`.
- The stop sequence goes in `src/process.rs`, next to the Unix one that
  sends `SIGTERM` and waits `GRACE`.
- The refusal is checked where `args` are quoted into the command line,
  before `CreateProcessW`.

## Done when

- On Windows CI, a console child that handles Ctrl-Break by exiting stops
  without `TerminateJobObject`, and one that ignores it is ended after 5
  seconds. Both report `timed-out`.
- On Windows CI, `run(command("echo.bat", ["a&b"]))` is `invalid-argument`
  naming `a&b`, and `run(command("echo.bat", ["ab"]))` runs.
- The "Implemented" note of the companion note no longer lists either rule
  as missing. The [[HQL-0064]] changelog and `CHANGELOG.md` say so.
